Note: Flow Standard Library — @core plus the broader library: music-typed
Note: overloads, unit conversions, notation helpers and @bars.
Note: The C# implementations are linked at runtime.

use "@core"
use "@bars"

internal proc str (Note: value)
internal proc str (Bar: value)
internal proc str (Semitone: value)
internal proc str (Cent: value)
internal proc str (Millisecond: value)
internal proc str (Second: value)
internal proc str (Decibel: value)
Note: sweep-0614 — Hertz prints with "Hz" suffix; dedicated overload disambiguates str(Float)/str(Double) (HertzType.IsCompatibleWith covers both)
internal proc str (Hertz: value)
Note: Phase 45 D-14 — Beat prints as a plain double (no "b" suffix); dedicated overload disambiguates str(Float)/str(Double)
internal proc str (Beat: value)
internal proc str (Sequence: value)
internal proc str (Chord: value)
internal proc str (Section: value)
internal proc str (Song: value)
Note: Tuning ((loadScala) output) string form
internal proc str (Tuning: value)

Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-04 (D-08/D-09/D-10) — explicit-conversion builtins.
Note: 6 forward (db/hz/ms/sec/cents/semitones) + 4 reverse (double/float/int/long
Note: × 6 music types) = 50 always-available overloads. Mode-independent per D-09
Note: so composers can test-drive conversions one call at a time when refactoring
Note: toward `enable strict;`. (semitones x) is Int-ONLY per D-08 (whole-numbers-by-
Note: design); Float/Double/Long inputs fall through to "No matching overload" in
Note: BOTH modes. C# implementations: flow-lang/StandardLibrary/ConversionFunctions.cs.

Note: -- Forward direction: raw numeric (+ idempotent target) → tagged music type
